Level1 Fixed Color Fill =
SWITCH (
    MAX ( 'MappedParameter'[Category] ),
    "PLACEHOLDER_VALUE_1", "#01B8AA",
    "PLACEHOLDER_VALUE_2", "#FD625E",
    "PLACEHOLDER_VALUE_3", "#F2C80F",
    BLANK () // falls back to level1DefaultFillColor in the spec -- see below
)
// Level1's field parameter is 'MappedParameter'[Category] -- the SAME
// table the aster plot's own Category role already uses (per the report
// author). Not a new table; see category-three-field-parameter.dax for
// the one genuinely new field parameter this visual needs (Level3's
// MappedParameterThree), and its comments for the shared-slicer
// implication of reusing MappedParameter/MappedParameterTwo here for
// Level1/Level2.
//
// One of THREE near-identical measures this visual needs -- copy this
// same SWITCH shape for Level 2 and Level 3, swapping the field parameter
// reference and giving each its OWN unique measure name (DAX measure
// names are unique per model, per docs/patterns.md's "Shared data model"
// section):
//   Level2 Fixed Color Fill = SWITCH ( MAX ( 'MappedParameterTwo'[Category2] ), ... )
//   Level3 Fixed Color Fill = SWITCH ( MAX ( 'MappedParameterThree'[Category3] ), ... )
// The SWITCH branches themselves (category values -> hex colors) are
// still placeholders above -- replace with this report's real category
// values once known; they aren't the same across levels since each level
// is a different grouping.
//
// Bind to Level1ColorOverrideFill (rename for this visual -- see
// spec/circle-packing.vg.json's field-mapping adapter, which maps
// Level1ColorOverrideFill -> the internal Level1FillOverride role).
// Falls back to level1DefaultFillColor when unbound or BLANK() -- leaving
// BLANK() as the final SWITCH branch (rather than a fallback color
// literal) lets the spec's own isValid() check apply the param instead,
// so the fallback color stays a spec-level setting rather than needing to
// be duplicated inside every DAX measure.
//
// Uses MAX, not SELECTEDVALUE or ALLSELECTED -- 'MappedParameter'[Category]
// is CONFIRMED composite-keyed (Power BI links a field parameter's
// Value/Fields/Order columns together as "Group By Columns"; a
// filter-context function on just one throws "part of composite key" --
// see visuals/aster-plot/dax/measure-a-color-gradient.dax for the full
// writeup). MappedParameterTwo/MappedParameterThree are presumed the same
// (every field parameter table behaves this way), but not each
// individually re-confirmed.
